{"id":"seats-held-over","title":"Seats held over past their term, and seats left vacant","question":"How many seats on City boards and commissions are vacant, or still occupied by a member whose term has expired, and whose job is it to fill them?","finding":"The Clerk of the Board’s vacancy notices (dated 2025-01-29 to 2026-10-20) list 943 seats on 100 bodies: 240 are printed as vacant and 63 more as vacant with the former member holding over. Of 483 seats the Board fills, 153 are vacant and 45 held over (41.0% not filled). Of 211 seats the Mayor fills, 48 are vacant and 13 held over (28.9% not filled). Of 20 seats the President of the Board of Supervisors fills, 1 is vacant and 1 held over (10.0% not filled). 53 of the 62 holdovers with a printed expiry date had run more than a year past it when the notice was dated; the longest is 4,650 days (Sweatfree Procurement Advisory Group, term expired 2012-05-07). 7 vacant seats are first appointments to a new body, and 24 seats print a named holder whose term end is earlier than the notice’s own date without calling the member a holdover. The Commission Streamlining Task Force’s workbook of January 2026 counts 230 vacant seats among 1,533 on the 121 bodies for which it gives both numbers.","how":"Every seat row of the Clerk’s “Vacancy Notice” pages. A seat is “vacant” when the holder column begins with the word VACANT, and “held over” when the same cell also names a holdover member; the expiry date is the one the notice prints after “Term Expired”, and days past term are counted from that date to the notice’s own “Updated” date. Appointing authorities are grouped from the notice’s own label: BOS, Mayor, BOS President, the two jointly, any other officer or department, or none printed. The first rows total each authority; the rows below list bodies with at least one holdover or three vacancies, most holdovers first.","limits":"These are the Clerk’s own notices, so the counts are official, but they are snapshots with different dates and a seat may have been filled since. A holdover is the notice’s own word for a member who keeps serving after the term ended; whether the law for that body allows it is not something these files state. A vacancy has ordinary causes: a new body not yet appointed, a seat with narrow qualifications, a resignation last month, or a body the Commission Streamlining Task Force has proposed to wind down. Commissions the Mayor fills without a Board vacancy notice are not covered. Being connected is not being corrupt, and nothing here says a vacancy or a holdover benefits anyone.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"authority","t":"Appointing authority, as the notice prints it","type":"text"},{"k":"body","t":"Body","type":"text"},{"k":"seats","t":"Seats","type":"int"},{"k":"filled","t":"Filled","type":"int"},{"k":"vacant","t":"Vacant","type":"int"},{"k":"heldOver","t":"Held over past term end","type":"int"},{"k":"notFilled","t":"Share vacant or held over","type":"pct"},{"k":"median","t":"Typical days past term end","type":"days"},{"k":"longest","t":"Longest","type":"days"},{"k":"expired","t":"That term expired","type":"date"},{"k":"pastEnd","t":"Named holders past the printed term end","type":"int"},{"k":"asOf","t":"Notice dated","type":"date"},{"k":"notice","t":"Notice","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"authority":"Board of Supervisors","body":"All bodies with a notice","seats":483,"filled":285,"vacant":153,"heldOver":45,"notFilled":0.4099,"median":407,"longest":2599,"expired":"2018-11-19","pastEnd":8,"asOf":"2026-10-20","notice":null},{"authority":"Mayor","body":"All bodies with a notice","seats":211,"filled":150,"vacant":48,"heldOver":13,"notFilled":0.2891,"median":880,"longest":4650,"expired":"2012-05-07","pastEnd":12,"asOf":"2026-10-20","notice":null},{"authority":"President of the Board of Supervisors","body":"All bodies with a notice","seats":20,"filled":18,"vacant":1,"heldOver":1,"notFilled":0.1,"median":813,"longest":813,"expired":"2024-05-08","pastEnd":1,"asOf":"2